$ todoer add port-cli-parser -l rust-port 'Parse the arguments.'
.todoer/todos/port-cli-parser.md

$ todoer add port-config -l rust-port -l config -d port-cli-parser
.todoer/todos/port-config.md

$ echo 'From stdin.' | todoer add release-v1 -d .todoer/todos/port-config.md
.todoer/todos/release-v1.md

$ todoer add port-cli-parser
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: the todo port-cli-parser exists - pick another name

$ todoer add
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: a todo needs a name - use todoer add <name> [-l label]... [-d name]... [-D label]... [text]

$ todoer add Fix_Login
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: "Fix_Login" is not a todo name - use fix-login

$ todoer add x -l Bad
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: "Bad" is not a label - use lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, with a letter or digit at each end

$ todoer add x -d missing
exit code: 1
--- stderr
error: there is no todo missing - run todoer ls

--- .todoer/todos/port-config.md
---
labels: [rust-port, config]
dependsOn: [port-cli-parser]
---

--- .todoer/todos/release-v1.md
---
dependsOn: [port-config]
---

From stdin.

$ todoer ls
available    port-cli-parser
blocked      port-config      waits for port-cli-parser
blocked      release-v1       waits for port-config

$ todoer ls --available
